{
  "title": "React Props",
  "duration": "30m",
  "cards": [
    {
      "id": "what-are-props",
      "title": "Understanding Props",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "3m",
      "content": "<p>Props (short for properties) are arguments passed into React components.</p>\n<p>Props are passed to components via HTML attributes and are <strong>read-only</strong>.</p>\n<pre><code><User name=\"Alice\" age={25} /></code></pre>"
    },
    {
      "id": "props-flow-mcq",
      "title": "Data Flow in React",
      "type": "mcq",
      "duration": "2m",
      "content": {
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "From child to parent"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "From parent to child"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Bi-directional"
          }
        ],
        "correctId": "b"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "destructuring-props",
      "title": "Destructuring Props",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "4m",
      "content": "<p>You can destructure props directly in the component parameter list for cleaner code.</p>\n<pre><code>function Product({ title, price }) {\n  return <h2>{title} - ${price}</h2>;\n}</code></pre>"
    },
    {
      "id": "fill-blank-props",
      "title": "Component Syntax",
      "type": "blank",
      "duration": "3m",
      "content": {
        "text": "To pass a prop named 'title' with value 'Hello' to a Card component, you write: <Card [blank]=\"Hello\" />",
        "answer": "title"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "match-props-types",
      "title": "Match Prop Concepts",
      "type": "match",
      "duration": "5m",
      "content": {
        "pairs": [
          {
            "left": "Props",
            "right": "Read-only data"
          },
          {
            "left": "State",
            "right": "Mutable internal data"
          },
          {
            "left": "Children",
            "right": "Special prop for nested elements"
          },
          {
            "left": "PropTypes",
            "right": "Runtime type checking"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "passing-order",
      "title": "Order of Operations",
      "type": "order",
      "duration": "5m",
      "content": {
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "1",
            "text": "Define the React component function accepting props"
          },
          {
            "id": "2",
            "text": "Destructure or access properties from the props object"
          },
          {
            "id": "3",
            "text": "Render the component inside a parent component with attributes"
          },
          {
            "id": "4",
            "text": "React mounts the component displaying the passed data"
          }
        ],
        "correctOrder": [
          "1",
          "2",
          "3",
          "4"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "props-summary",
      "title": "Summary",
      "type": "content",
      "duration": "3m",
      "content": "<p>Key takeaways:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Props make components reusable.</li>\n<li>Props flow downwards from parent to child.</li>\n<li>Props must never be modified inside the receiving component.</li>\n</ul>"
    }
  ]
}